/*
   Question bank for the page quizzes. Each page's "Quiz me" runs its memory questions,
   then reasoning, then analysis, shuffled within each kind. The quiz is part of the page's teaching,
   so the explanations matter as much as the questions.

   Each question:
     id          unique, stable (used to remember results between visits)
     condition   matches an article id in index.html
     kind        "memory" (short what or which recall), "reasoning" (why, how, mechanism, or
                 what to do next), or "analysis" (a case or data to interpret, relying on inference)
     stem        the question; HTML allowed (paragraphs, tables). Older questions put the
                 question itself in leadIn
     leadIn      optional; the question, when the stem is a vignette
     options     five answer choices, shuffled when shown, so nothing may refer to a letter
     answer      index of the correct option
     explanation why and how the answer is right, written as teaching; HTML allowed
     notes       { optionIndex: "why this option is wrong, or when it would be right" } for
                 every wrong option; never on the correct one
     info        optional extra context beyond the course material, shown as "Additional information"
     set         optional; questions sharing a case use the same set name and stay together, in order
     passage     the shared case, on the first question of a set only; HTML allowed
*/

