<p>Ultrasound: a large stone impacted in the gallbladder neck, a thick gallbladder wall, and pericholecystic fluid. The intrahepatic ducts and common hepatic duct are dilated, but the common bile duct below the cystic duct is of normal width and contains no stones.</p>
